IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`
IMPORT `sca-p1-preliminary`

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition -- LAYER 1, PART 4 (first part): CIVIL JURISDICTION OF DISTRICT COURTS (ss 19 to 49B).
-- The District Court limit is a parameter of each function that needs it ("the District Court limit in dollars"): the caller takes it from
-- `s 2 "District Court limit" the amount in dollars` (the Act's $250,000 unless an order under s 30 specifies another amount).
-- Each section answers for itself (option C of the ruling E1).  Where a reader needs the sections read together, the one function that does so by hand
-- is `s 19 a District Court has jurisdiction over the action`, and the fork register says so (option B as guidance for hand-gathering only).
-- A "no" is given only where the text says no in its own words; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING".

§ `Section 19 -- general civil jurisdiction`

-- src:862 | 19.—(1) A District Court exercising civil jurisdiction is a court of
-- src:863 | record.
@ref s 19(1) (src:862-863)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
      `it is exercising civil jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(1) the court is a court of record` MEANS
    IF court EQUALS `District Court` AND `it is exercising civil jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "A District Court exercising civil jurisdiction" and says nothing of another court or of civil jurisdiction not so exercised
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:865 | (2) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), a District Court has all the
-- src:866 | jurisdiction of the General Division of the High Court to hear and try
-- src:867 | any action in personam where —
-- src:869 | (a) the defendant is served with an originating claim or any
-- src:870 | other originating process —
-- src:872 | (i) in Singapore in the manner prescribed by Rules of
-- src:873 | Court; or
-- src:875 | (ii) outside Singapore in the circumstances authorised by
-- src:876 | and in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court; or
-- src:880 | (b) the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of a District
-- src:881 | Court.
@ref s 19(2)(a)(i), (a)(ii) and (b) (src:865-881)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(2) a District Court has the jurisdiction of the General Division of the High Court to hear and try the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of jurisdiction "to hear and try any action in personam"
        IF NOT (proceeding's `the action is in personam`) THEN NOTHING
        IF proceeding's `the defendant was served in Singapore in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court`
           OR proceeding's `the defendant was served outside Singapore in the circumstances authorised by and in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court`
           OR proceeding's `the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the court asked about`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where — (a) the defendant is served ... (i) in Singapore ... or (ii) outside Singapore ...; or (b) the defendant submits to the jurisdiction" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:885 | (3) Subject to section 28A of the Supreme Court of Judicature
-- src:886 | Act 1969 and any order under subsection (1) thereof, a District
-- src:887 | Court’s jurisdiction under subsection (2) does not include —
-- src:889 | (a) any supervisory jurisdiction or revisionary jurisdiction;
-- src:891 | (b) any jurisdiction relating to the judicial review of any act
-- src:892 | done or decision made by any person or authority,
-- src:893 | including the issue of any of the following prerogative
-- src:894 | orders:
-- src:896 | (i) a Mandatory Order;
-- src:901 | (ii) a Prohibiting Order;
-- src:903 | (iii) a Quashing Order;
-- src:905 | (iv) an Order for Review of Detention;
-- src:907 | (c) any jurisdiction vested exclusively in the General Division
-- src:908 | of the High Court, in a Family Court, in a Youth Court, in
-- src:909 | any other State Court, or in any judicial, quasi‑judicial or
-- src:910 | administrative tribunal, by written law;
-- src:914 | (ca) any jurisdiction to hear and try an action in passing off; and
-- src:918 | (d) any jurisdiction expressly excluded by written law.
@ref s 19(3)(a) to (d) (src:885-918)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(3) the action falls within a class that subsection (3) excludes from a District Court's jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF proceeding's `the action is within a supervisory or revisionary jurisdiction`
       OR proceeding's `the action is for judicial review of an act or decision, including a Mandatory Order, a Prohibiting Order, a Quashing Order or an Order for Review of Detention`
       OR proceeding's `jurisdiction over the action is vested exclusively in the General Division of the High Court, a Family Court, a Youth Court, another State Court or a tribunal by written law`
       OR proceeding's `the action is in passing off`
       OR proceeding's `jurisdiction over the action is expressly excluded by written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- classifier fact, not a kind comment: no listed class applies to these facts; a plain yes/no about the facts, and the grant is s 19(2)

@ref s 19(3) (src:885-918)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(3) a District Court's jurisdiction under subsection (2) includes the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to section 28A of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 and any order under subsection (1) thereof"; that section and any order are not among the sources
        IF proceeding's `section 28A of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969, or an order under its subsection (1), affects the action` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a District Court’s jurisdiction under subsection (2) does not include — (a) any supervisory jurisdiction or revisionary jurisdiction; (b) any jurisdiction relating to the judicial review ...; (c) any jurisdiction vested exclusively ...; (ca) any jurisdiction to hear and try an action in passing off; and (d) any jurisdiction expressly excluded by written law"
        IF `s 19(3) the action falls within a class that subsection (3) excludes from a District Court's jurisdiction` proceeding EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an action outside those classes is not mentioned in subsection (3), which grants nothing
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:922 | (4) Subject to sections 22 and 23, a District Court’s jurisdiction
-- src:923 | under subsection (2) does not include jurisdiction to hear and try any
-- src:924 | action where —
-- src:926 | (a) the amount claimed in the action exceeds the District Court
-- src:927 | limit; or
-- src:929 | (b) any remedy or relief sought in the action is in respect of a
-- src:930 | subject matter the value of which exceeds the District
-- src:931 | Court limit.
@ref s 19(4)(a) and (b) (src:922-931)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(4) the amount claimed or the value of the subject matter of the remedy or relief exceeds the District Court limit` MEANS
    IF proceeding's `the amount claimed in dollars` GREATER THAN `the District Court limit in dollars`
       OR proceeding's `the value in dollars of the subject matter of any remedy or relief sought` GREATER THAN `the District Court limit in dollars`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- classifier fact, not a kind comment: neither figure exceeds the limit ("exceeds" means more than the figure)

@ref s 19(4) (src:922-931)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(4) a District Court's jurisdiction under subsection (2) includes the action despite its amount or value` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to sections 22 and 23"; where the claimant has abandoned the excess or the parties have agreed, the bar is lifted and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA); sections 22 and 23 are the grants
        IF `s 19(4) the amount claimed or the value of the subject matter of the remedy or relief exceeds the District Court limit` proceeding `the District Court limit in dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND (proceeding's `the claimant has abandoned the excess amount or the remedy or relief` OR proceeding's `the parties agreed, by a memorandum signed by them or their solicitors, that the court is to have jurisdiction`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a District Court’s jurisdiction under subsection (2) does not include jurisdiction to hear and try any action where — (a) the amount claimed in the action exceeds the District Court limit; or (b) any remedy or relief sought in the action is in respect of a subject matter the value of which exceeds the District Court limit"
        IF `s 19(4) the amount claimed or the value of the subject matter of the remedy or relief exceeds the District Court limit` proceeding `the District Court limit in dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an action within the limit is not mentioned in subsection (4), which grants nothing
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:937 | (6) Without limiting subsection (2), a District Court has such
-- src:938 | jurisdiction as is vested in it by any other written law.
@ref s 19(6) (src:937-938)
GIVEN `another written law vests the jurisdiction in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(6) a District Court has the jurisdiction vested in it by another written law` MEANS
    IF `another written law vests the jurisdiction in a District Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such jurisdiction as is vested in it by any other written law" says nothing of jurisdiction no written law vests
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 22 and 23 -- abandoning part of a claim; jurisdiction by agreement`

-- src:947 | 22.—(1) Where —
-- src:949 | (a) the amount claimed in an action exceeds the District Court
-- src:950 | limit, or any remedy or relief sought in an action is in
-- src:951 | respect of a subject matter the value of which exceeds the
-- src:952 | District Court limit; and
-- src:957 | (b) a District Court would have jurisdiction under
-- src:958 | section 19(2) to hear and try the action if the amount or
-- src:959 | value (as the case may be) did not exceed the District Court
-- src:960 | limit,
-- src:962 | the claimant may abandon the excess amount or that remedy or relief,
-- src:963 | as the case may be, and thereupon a District Court has jurisdiction
-- src:964 | under section 19(2) to hear and try the action, except that the claimant
-- src:965 | cannot in that action —
-- src:967 | (c) recover an amount exceeding the District Court limit; and
-- src:969 | (d) obtain any remedy or relief in respect of the subject matter
-- src:970 | the value of which exceeds the District Court limit.
@ref s 22(1)(a) to (d) (src:947-970)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) the claimant may abandon the excess amount or the remedy or relief` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where — (a) the amount claimed ... exceeds the District Court limit, or any remedy or relief ... exceeds the District Court limit" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `s 19(4) the amount claimed or the value of the subject matter of the remedy or relief exceeds the District Court limit` proceeding `the District Court limit in dollars` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- (b): a District Court would have jurisdiction under section 19(2) if the amount or value did not exceed the limit
        IF `s 19(2) a District Court has the jurisdiction of the General Division of the High Court to hear and try the action` proceeding EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `s 19(3) the action falls within a class that subsection (3) excludes from a District Court's jurisdiction` proceeding EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where ... (b) a District Court would have jurisdiction under section 19(2) to hear and try the action if the amount or value ... did not exceed the District Court limit" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 22(1) (src:947-970)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) this section gives a District Court jurisdiction under section 19(2) to hear and try the action` MEANS
    IF `s 22(1) the claimant may abandon the excess amount or the remedy or relief` proceeding `the District Court limit in dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND proceeding's `the claimant has abandoned the excess amount or the remedy or relief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant may abandon the excess amount ... and thereupon a District Court has jurisdiction" (this section gives no jurisdiction on these facts; "thereupon" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05 (c))
         JUST FALSE

@ref s 22(1)(c) (src:947-970)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the amount the claimant seeks to recover in the action in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1)(c) the claimant may recover the amount in the action` MEANS
    IF `s 22(1) this section gives a District Court jurisdiction under section 19(2) to hear and try the action` proceeding `the District Court limit in dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the amount the claimant seeks to recover in the action in dollars` GREATER THAN `the District Court limit in dollars`
    THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant cannot in that action — (c) recover an amount exceeding the District Court limit"
         JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception reaches only a claimant whose jurisdiction rests on this section and who seeks more than the limit; for any other case it says nothing
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 22(1)(d) (src:947-970)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the value in dollars of the subject matter of the remedy or relief the claimant seeks` IS A NUMBER
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(1)(d) the claimant may obtain the remedy or relief in the action` MEANS
    IF `s 22(1) this section gives a District Court jurisdiction under section 19(2) to hear and try the action` proceeding `the District Court limit in dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND `the value in dollars of the subject matter of the remedy or relief the claimant seeks` GREATER THAN `the District Court limit in dollars`
    THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant cannot in that action — ... (d) obtain any remedy or relief in respect of the subject matter the value of which exceeds the District Court limit"
         JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception reaches only a claimant whose jurisdiction rests on this section and who seeks relief for a subject matter above the limit
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:976 | (2) Where a District Court has jurisdiction to hear and try an action
-- src:977 | by virtue of this section, the judgment of the court in the action is a
-- src:978 | full discharge of all demands in respect of the cause of action.
@ref s 22(2) (src:976-978)
GIVEN `the District Court has jurisdiction to hear and try the action by virtue of section 22` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) the judgment of the court in the action is a full discharge of all demands in respect of the cause of action` MEANS
    IF `the District Court has jurisdiction to hear and try the action by virtue of section 22`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a District Court has jurisdiction to hear and try an action by virtue of this section, the judgment ... is a full discharge" (this subsection gives no discharge on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:982 | 23. Where the parties to an action agree, by a memorandum signed
-- src:983 | by them or their respective solicitors, a District Court has jurisdiction
-- src:984 | under section 19(2) to hear and try the action even though —
-- src:986 | (a) the amount claimed in the action exceeds the District Court
-- src:987 | limit; or
-- src:989 | (b) any remedy or relief sought in the action is in respect of a
-- src:990 | subject matter the value of which exceeds the District
-- src:991 | Court limit.
@ref s 23 (src:982-991)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23 this section gives a District Court jurisdiction under section 19(2) to hear and try the action even though its amount or value exceeds the District Court limit` MEANS
    IF proceeding's `the parties agreed, by a memorandum signed by them or their solicitors, that the court is to have jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the parties to an action agree, by a memorandum signed by them or their respective solicitors, a District Court has jurisdiction" (this section gives no jurisdiction on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

§ `Section 19 read together with sections 22 and 23 (gathered by hand)`

@ref s 19, s 22 and s 23 read together (src:862-991)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 a District Court has jurisdiction over the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (3) is "Subject to section 28A of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 and any order under subsection (1) thereof", which are not among the sources
        IF `s 19(3) the action falls within a class that subsection (3) excludes from a District Court's jurisdiction` proceeding EQUALS JUST TRUE AND proceeding's `section 28A of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969, or an order under its subsection (1), affects the action` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 19(3) "does not include"
        IF `s 19(3) the action falls within a class that subsection (3) excludes from a District Court's jurisdiction` proceeding EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 19(2) is for "any action in personam"
        IF `s 19(2) a District Court has the jurisdiction of the General Division of the High Court to hear and try the action` proceeding EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 19(2) "where" is not met
        IF `s 19(2) a District Court has the jurisdiction of the General Division of the High Court to hear and try the action` proceeding EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- the amount and value are within the limit: section 19(2) holds and neither (3) nor (4) takes the action out
        IF `s 19(4) the amount claimed or the value of the subject matter of the remedy or relief exceeds the District Court limit` proceeding `the District Court limit in dollars` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- over the limit but the claimant has abandoned the excess (s 22) or the parties have agreed (s 23)
        IF `s 22(1) this section gives a District Court jurisdiction under section 19(2) to hear and try the action` proceeding `the District Court limit in dollars` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 23 this section gives a District Court jurisdiction under section 19(2) to hear and try the action even though its amount or value exceeds the District Court limit` proceeding EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 19(4) "does not include jurisdiction to hear and try any action where — (a) the amount claimed ... exceeds the District Court limit; or (b) any remedy or relief sought ... exceeds the District Court limit"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 25 to 29 -- recovery of immovable property, equity, distress and interpleader`

-- src:999 | 25. Without limiting section 19, a District Court has jurisdiction
-- src:1000 | under section 19(2) to hear and try any action for the recovery of
-- src:1001 | immovable property with or without a claim for rent or mesne profits
-- src:1002 | and whether or not the title to the property is in dispute, where —
-- src:1007 | (a) the annual value of the property appearing in the Valuation
-- src:1008 | List prepared under section 10 of the Property Tax
-- src:1009 | Act 1960 does not exceed the District Court limit;
-- src:1011 | (b) the annual rent payable by the tenant does not exceed the
-- src:1012 | District Court limit or the monthly rent payable by the
-- src:1013 | tenant does not exceed one-twelfth of the District Court
-- src:1014 | limit; or
-- src:1016 | (c) if the annual value, annual rent or monthly rent cannot be
-- src:1017 | ascertained, the last transacted price of the property does
-- src:1018 | not exceed 10 times the District Court limit.
@ref s 25(a) to (c) (src:999-1018)
GIVEN property IS A `Recovery of immovable property`
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25 this section gives a District Court jurisdiction to hear and try the action for the recovery of immovable property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is about "any action for the recovery of immovable property"
        IF NOT (property's `it is an action for the recovery of immovable property`) THEN NOTHING
        -- (a) the annual value of the property appearing in the Valuation List does not exceed the District Court limit
        IF `s 25 the amount is within the limit` (property's `the annual value of the property appearing in the Valuation List`) `the District Court limit in dollars` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (b) the annual rent payable by the tenant does not exceed the District Court limit, or the monthly rent does not exceed one-twelfth of it
        IF `s 25 the amount is within the limit` (property's `the annual rent payable by the tenant`) `the District Court limit in dollars` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 25 the amount is within the limit` (property's `the monthly rent payable by the tenant`) (`the District Court limit in dollars` DIVIDED BY 12) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- (c) if the annual value, annual rent or monthly rent cannot be ascertained, the last transacted price does not exceed 10 times the District Court limit
        IF `s 25 none of the annual value, annual rent or monthly rent can be ascertained` property
           AND `s 25 the amount is within the limit` (property's `the last transacted price of the property`) (10 TIMES `the District Court limit in dollars`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has jurisdiction ... where —" none of (a), (b) and (c) holds (this section gives no jurisdiction on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 25 (src:999-1018)
GIVEN amount IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      ceiling IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25 the amount is within the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER amount
    WHEN JUST x THEN x AT MOST ceiling
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

@ref s 25(c) (src:999-1018)
GIVEN property IS A `Recovery of immovable property`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25 none of the annual value, annual rent or monthly rent can be ascertained` MEANS
    CONSIDER property's `the annual value of the property appearing in the Valuation List`
    WHEN JUST x THEN FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER property's `the annual rent payable by the tenant`
        WHEN JUST y THEN FALSE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            CONSIDER property's `the monthly rent payable by the tenant`
            WHEN JUST z THEN FALSE
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

-- src:1024 | 26. Without limiting section 19, a District Court has jurisdiction
-- src:1025 | under section 19(2) to hear and try any of the following proceedings:
-- src:1027 | (a) [Deleted by Act 27 of 2014]
-- src:1029 | (b) proceedings for the execution of any trust or for a
-- src:1030 | declaration that a trust subsists, where the amount or
-- src:1031 | value of the property subject, or alleged to be subject, to the
-- src:1032 | trust does not exceed the District Court limit;
-- src:1034 | (c) proceedings for foreclosure or redemption of any mortgage
-- src:1035 | or for enforcing any charge or lien, where the amount
-- src:1036 | owing in respect of the mortgage, charge or lien does not
-- src:1037 | exceed the District Court limit;
-- src:1039 | (d) proceedings for the specific performance, or for the
-- src:1040 | rectification, delivery up or cancellation of any
-- src:1041 | agreement for the sale, purchase or lease of any property,
-- src:1042 | where, in the case of a sale or purchase, the purchase
-- src:1043 | money or, in the case of a lease, the amount or value of the
-- src:1044 | property does not exceed the District Court limit;
-- src:1046 | (e) [Deleted by Act 27 of 2014]
-- src:1048 | (f) proceedings for the dissolution or winding up of any
-- src:1049 | partnership (other than a limited liability partnership
-- src:1050 | registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships
-- src:1051 | Act 2005), whether or not the existence of the
-- src:1056 | partnership is in dispute, where the amount or value of all
-- src:1057 | the assets of the partnership does not exceed the District
-- src:1058 | Court limit;
-- src:1060 | (g) proceedings for relief against fraud or mistake where the
-- src:1061 | damage sustained or the amount or value of the estate or
-- src:1062 | fund in respect of which relief is sought does not exceed
-- src:1063 | the District Court limit.
@ref s 26(b) to (g) (src:1024-1063)
GIVEN proceeding IS AN `Equity proceeding`
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26 this section gives a District Court jurisdiction to hear and try the proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any of the following proceedings" lists five kinds (paragraphs (a) and (e) are deleted) and does not say "only"
        IF proceeding's kind EQUALS `Another kind of proceeding` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(other than a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005)" takes it out of the grant (QE: a limit on a grant, so NOTHING)
        IF proceeding's kind EQUALS `Dissolution or winding up of a partnership` AND proceeding's `the partnership is a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` THEN NOTHING
        IF proceeding's `the amount or value that the paragraph measures` AT MOST `the District Court limit in dollars` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the amount or value ... does not exceed the District Court limit" (this section gives no jurisdiction on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1071 | 28. A District Court has jurisdiction under the Distress Act 1934 in
-- src:1072 | all cases where the amount of rent distrained or to be distrained does
-- src:1073 | not exceed the District Court limit.
@ref s 28 (src:1071-1073)
GIVEN `the amount of rent distrained or to be distrained in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28 this section gives a District Court jurisdiction under the Distress Act 1934` MEANS
    IF `the amount of rent distrained or to be distrained in dollars` AT MOST `the District Court limit in dollars`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in all cases where the amount of rent distrained or to be distrained does not exceed the District Court limit" (this section gives no jurisdiction on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:1077 | 29.—(1) Without limiting section 19, a District Court has
-- src:1078 | jurisdiction under section 19(2) to grant relief by way of
-- src:1079 | interpleader —
-- src:1081 | (a) where a bailiff of a District Court is charged with the
-- src:1082 | execution of any writ or order of the Court and claim is
-- src:1083 | made to any money or other movable property taken or
-- src:1084 | intended to be taken in execution of the writ or order, or to
-- src:1085 | the proceeds or value of any such property, by any person
-- src:1086 | other than the person against whom the writ or order was
-- src:1087 | issued or made; and
-- src:1089 | (b) where the person seeking relief is under liability for any
-- src:1090 | debt, money, or other movable property of which the
-- src:1091 | amount or value does not exceed the District Court limit
-- src:1092 | and for or in respect of which the person has been or
-- src:1093 | expects to be sued by 2 or more parties making adverse
-- src:1094 | claims thereto.
@ref s 29(1)(a) and (b) (src:1077-1094)
GIVEN claim IS AN `Interpleader claim`
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) this section gives a District Court jurisdiction to grant relief by way of interpleader` MEANS
    IF (claim's `a bailiff of a District Court is charged with the execution of a writ or order of the Court and a person other than the person against whom it was issued claims the money or movable property taken or intended to be taken, or its proceeds or value`)
       OR ((claim's `the person seeking relief is under liability for a debt, money or other movable property and has been or expects to be sued by 2 or more parties making adverse claims to it`)
           AND (claim's `the amount or value of that debt, money or movable property` AT MOST `the District Court limit in dollars`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "has jurisdiction ... to grant relief by way of interpleader — (a) where a bailiff ... ; and (b) where the person seeking relief is under liability ... of which the amount or value does not exceed the District Court limit" (each head is read as its own ground, (a) holding alone or (b) holding alone within the limit, and the District Court limit is tested only on (b), fork F-S29-AND; when neither head is met, a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:1098 | (2) If it appears to the General Division of the High Court that any
-- src:1099 | proceedings in the General Division of the High Court by way of
-- src:1100 | interpleader, in which the amount in dispute or value of the subject
-- src:1105 | matter does not exceed the District Court limit, may be more
-- src:1106 | conveniently tried in a District Court, the General Division of the
-- src:1107 | High Court may at any time order that the proceedings be transferred
-- src:1108 | to a District Court.
@ref s 29(2) (src:1098-1108)
GIVEN `the proceedings in the General Division of the High Court are by way of interpleader` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `it appears to the General Division of the High Court that the proceedings may be more conveniently tried in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the District Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(2) the General Division of the High Court may order that the proceedings be transferred to a District Court` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings in the General Division of the High Court are by way of interpleader`
       AND `the amount in dispute or the value of the subject matter in dollars` AT MOST `the District Court limit in dollars`
       AND `it appears to the General Division of the High Court that the proceedings may be more conveniently tried in a District Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If it appears to the General Division of the High Court that any proceedings ... by way of interpleader, in which the amount in dispute or value of the subject matter does not exceed the District Court limit, may be more conveniently tried in a District Court, the General Division of the High Court may ... order" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
         JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 31 to 35 -- the powers of a District Court and of its officers`

-- src:1121 | 31.—(1) A District Court, as regards any action within its
-- src:1122 | jurisdiction, is in any proceedings before it —
-- src:1124 | (a) to grant such relief, redress or remedy or combination of
-- src:1125 | remedies, either absolute or conditional; and
-- src:1127 | (b) to give such and the like effect to every ground of defence
-- src:1128 | or counterclaim equitable or legal,
-- src:1130 | as ought to be granted or given in the like action by the General
-- src:1131 | Division of the High Court and in as full and ample a manner.
@ref s 31(1)(a) and (b) (src:1121-1131)
GIVEN `the action is within the jurisdiction of the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `Power of a court in a civil action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the District Court has the power in the proceedings before it` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `Grant any relief, redress or remedy, or combination of remedies, absolute or conditional` THEN `s 31 the power is conferred if the action is within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the District Court`
    WHEN `Give effect to every ground of defence or counterclaim, equitable or legal` THEN `s 31 the power is conferred if the action is within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the District Court`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) confers the two powers in paragraphs (a) and (b); the others are in subsection (2) or elsewhere
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 31 (src:1121-1131)
GIVEN `the action is within the jurisdiction of the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31 the power is conferred if the action is within the jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the action is within the jurisdiction of the District Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the powers are given "as regards any action within its jurisdiction"; the subsection says nothing of an action outside it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1135 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), a District Court, as regards any
-- src:1136 | action within its jurisdiction, has power —
-- src:1138 | (a) to grant an injunction whether or not any other relief is or
-- src:1139 | could be claimed;
-- src:1141 | (b) to make binding declarations of rights whether or not any
-- src:1142 | consequential relief is or could be claimed; and
-- src:1144 | (c) to order medical examination of a person who is a party to
-- src:1145 | any proceedings where the physical or mental condition of
-- src:1146 | the person is relevant to any matter in question in the
-- src:1147 | proceedings.
@ref s 31(2)(a) to (c) (src:1135-1147)
GIVEN `the action is within the jurisdiction of the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `Power of a court in a civil action`
      `the physical or mental condition of the person is relevant to any matter in question in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2) the District Court has the power as regards the action` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `Grant an injunction` THEN `s 31 the power is conferred if the action is within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the District Court`
    WHEN `Make a binding declaration of rights` THEN `s 31 the power is conferred if the action is within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the District Court`
    WHEN `Order the medical examination of a party` THEN
        IF NOT (`the physical or mental condition of the person is relevant to any matter in question in the proceedings`)
        THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to order medical examination of a person who is a party to any proceedings where the physical or mental condition of the person is relevant to any matter in question" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
             JUST FALSE
        ELSE `s 31 the power is conferred if the action is within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the District Court`
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Without limiting subsection (1)" - subsection (2) lists three powers and does not say a District Court has no other
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1156 | 32. A District Judge has power in any civil proceeding pending in a
-- src:1157 | District Court to make any order or to exercise any authority or
-- src:1158 | jurisdiction which, if it related to a proceeding pending in the General
-- src:1159 | Division of the High Court, might be made or exercised by a Judge
-- src:1160 | sitting in chambers in the General Division of the High Court.
@ref s 32 (src:1156-1160)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
      `it is a civil proceeding pending in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division of the High Court might make the order or exercise the authority in a like proceeding there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 32 the District Judge has power to make the order or exercise the authority or jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF holder EQUALS `District Judge` AND `it is a civil proceeding pending in a District Court` AND `a Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division of the High Court might make the order or exercise the authority in a like proceeding there`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is of "A District Judge" "in any civil proceeding pending in a District Court" and reaches what "a Judge sitting in chambers in the General Division" might do
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1166 | 33.—(1) In any proceedings, a District Judge may, if he or she
-- src:1167 | thinks fit on the application of any party, or on his or her own motion,
-- src:1168 | summon to his or her assistance, in such manner that is prescribed by
-- src:1169 | Rules of Court, one or more persons of skill and experience in the
-- src:1170 | matter to which the proceedings relate who may be willing to sit with
-- src:1171 | the District Judge and act as assessors.
@ref s 33(1) (src:1166-1171)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
      `the District Judge thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is on the application of a party or on his or her own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons have skill and experience in the matter to which the proceedings relate and are willing to sit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(1) the District Judge may summon the persons to assist and act as assessors` MEANS
    IF holder EQUALS `District Judge` AND `the District Judge thinks fit` AND `it is on the application of a party or on his or her own motion` AND `the persons have skill and experience in the matter to which the proceedings relate and are willing to sit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is the District Judge's, "if he or she thinks fit", over "persons of skill and experience in the matter ... who may be willing to sit"; the judgment of what is fit is the judge's
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1173 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), the remuneration of assessors for
-- src:1174 | sitting under this section is to be at such rate as may be prescribed by
-- src:1175 | Rules of Court and is to be costs in the proceedings unless otherwise
-- src:1176 | ordered by the District Judge.
@ref s 33(2) (src:1173-1176)
GIVEN `the assessors are summoned on the application of a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the District Judge has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(2) the remuneration of the assessors is costs in the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): subsection (2) is "Subject to subsection (3)", which deals with assessors summoned otherwise than on a party's application (see s 33(3))
        IF NOT (`the assessors are summoned on the application of a party to the proceedings`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to be costs in the proceedings unless otherwise ordered by the District Judge" (a deeming lifted by "unless": the requirement does not apply)
        IF `the District Judge has ordered otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1178 | (3) Where one or more assessors are summoned for the purposes of
-- src:1179 | this section otherwise than on the application of a party to the
