-- src:1181 | moneys provided by Parliament.
@ref s 33(3) (src:1178-1181)
GIVEN `the assessors are summoned otherwise than on the application of a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(3) the remuneration of the assessor is payable out of moneys provided by Parliament` MEANS
    IF `the assessors are summoned otherwise than on the application of a party to the proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where one or more assessors are summoned ... otherwise than on the application of a party ..., the remuneration of any such assessor is payable out of moneys provided by Parliament" (this subsection gives no such payment on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:1183 | (4) Where any person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor,
-- src:1184 | objection to the person, either personally or in respect of the person’s
-- src:1185 | qualification, may be taken by any party in the prescribed manner.
@ref s 33(4) (src:1183-1185)
GIVEN `the person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection is taken by a party in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 33(4) a party may object to the person, personally or in respect of qualification` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor, objection ... may be taken" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF NOT (`the person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the objection is taken by a party in the prescribed manner` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the objection is to be taken "in the prescribed manner"; the manner is in Rules of Court, which are not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1189 | 34. Any jurisdiction and powers conferred on a District Court by
-- src:1190 | this Act or any other written law relating to civil proceedings may be
-- src:1191 | exercised, to the extent authorised by this Act or any other written law
-- src:1192 | or Rules of Court, by the registrar.
@ref s 34 (src:1189-1192)
GIVEN holder IS A `Holder of an office or post`
      `the exercise is to the extent authorised by this Act, any other written law or Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34 the registrar may exercise the jurisdiction and powers conferred on a District Court relating to civil proceedings` MEANS
    IF (holder EQUALS `Registrar of the State Courts` OR holder EQUALS `Deputy registrar of the State Courts`) AND `the exercise is to the extent authorised by this Act, any other written law or Rules of Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent authorised by this Act or any other written law or Rules of Court"; what they authorise is not among the sources
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1196 | 35. A cause of action must not be divided for the purpose of
