        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1227 | 39.—(1) Where an action is commenced in the General Division of
-- src:1228 | the High Court which could have been commenced in a State Court,
-- src:1229 | then, subject to subsections (3) and (4), the claimant —
-- src:1231 | (a) if he or she recovers a sum not exceeding the District Court
-- src:1232 | limit, is not entitled to any more costs of the action than
-- src:1233 | those to which he or she would have been entitled if the
-- src:1234 | action had been brought in a District Court; and
-- src:1236 | (b) if he or she recovers a sum not exceeding the Magistrate’s
-- src:1237 | Court limit, is not entitled to any more costs of the action
-- src:1238 | than those to which he or she would have been entitled if
-- src:1239 | the action had been brought in a Magistrate’s Court.
@ref s 39(1)(a) and (b) (src:1227-1239)
GIVEN `it is an action commenced in the General Division of the High Court which could have been commenced in a State Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum the claimant recovers in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `section 39(4) or (5) lifts the limit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(1) the claimant is entitled to more costs than an action brought in a State Court with that limit would carry` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is about "an action ... commenced in the General Division of the High Court which could have been commenced in a State Court"
        IF NOT (`it is an action commenced in the General Division of the High Court which could have been commenced in a State Court`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to subsections (3) and (4)" and the section "does not apply" to proceedings by the Government (subsection (5)); the result then turns on an order of the court
        IF `section 39(4) or (5) lifts the limit` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant — (a) if he or she recovers a sum not exceeding the District Court limit, is not entitled to any more costs of the action than those to which he or she would have been entitled if the action had been brought in a District Court" (and likewise (b) for the Magistrate's Court limit)
        IF `the sum the claimant recovers in dollars` AT MOST `the limit in dollars` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the claimant who recovers more than the limit is outside paragraphs (a) and (b)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1245 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a) and (b), a claimant is
-- src:1246 | treated as recovering the full amount recoverable in respect of his or
-- src:1247 | her claim without regard to any deduction made in respect of
