GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 39(2) the claimant is treated as recovering the full amount recoverable without regard to the deduction` MEANS
    IF `the deduction was for contributory negligence or for another matter that does not fall to be taken into account in determining whether the action could have been commenced in a State Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the treatment is "without regard to any deduction made in respect of contributory negligence ... or otherwise in respect of matters not falling to be taken into account"; another deduction is not mentioned
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 39(2) (src:1245-1254)
GIVEN `the full amount recoverable in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the deduction in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 39(2) the sum the claimant is treated as recovering in dollars` MEANS
    -- the full amount recoverable, "without regard to any deduction": the deduction is an input only so that the question can be asked in the Act's own terms, and it is not subtracted
    `the full amount recoverable in dollars`

