§ `Sections 42 to 45 -- finality, satisfaction and enforcement of District Court judgments`

-- src:1324 | 42. Every judgment and order of a District Court exercising civil
-- src:1325 | jurisdiction is, except as provided by this Act, any other written law
-- src:1326 | or Rules of Court, final and conclusive between the parties.
@ref s 42 (src:1324-1326)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
      `it is a judgment or order of the court exercising civil jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act, any other written law or Rules of Court provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 42 the judgment or order is final and conclusive between the parties` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "Every judgment and order of a District Court exercising civil jurisdiction"
        IF NOT (court EQUALS `District Court` AND `it is a judgment or order of the court exercising civil jurisdiction`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, except as provided by this Act, any other written law or Rules of Court, final and conclusive" (a deeming lifted by "except": the requirement does not apply)
        IF `this Act, any other written law or Rules of Court provide otherwise` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1330 | 43.—(1) Where a judgment is given or an order is made by a
-- src:1331 | District Court under which any sum of money is payable, whether by
-- src:1332 | way of satisfaction of the claim or counterclaim in the proceedings or
-- src:1333 | by way of costs or otherwise, the Court may, as it thinks fit, order the
-- src:1334 | money to be paid either —
-- src:1336 | (a) in one sum, whether immediately or within a period fixed
-- src:1337 | by the Court; or
-- src:1339 | (b) by the instalments payable at the times fixed by the Court.
@ref s 43(1)(a) and (b) (src:1330-1339)
GIVEN `a judgment is given or an order is made by a District Court under which any sum of money is payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks fit to order payment in one sum or by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(1) the District Court may order the money to be paid in one sum or by instalments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a judgment is given or an order is made by a District Court under which any sum of money is payable, ... the Court may, as it thinks fit, order" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF NOT (`a judgment is given or an order is made by a District Court under which any sum of money is payable`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the Court thinks fit to order payment in one sum or by instalments` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as it thinks fit"; the judgment is the Court's
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1341 | (2) If at any time it appears to the satisfaction of a District Court that
-- src:1342 | any party to any proceedings is unable from any cause to pay any sum
-- src:1343 | recovered against the party (whether by way of satisfaction of the
-- src:1344 | claim or counterclaim in the proceedings or by way of costs or
-- src:1345 | otherwise) or any instalment thereof, the Court may, in its discretion,
-- src:1346 | suspend or stay any judgment or order given or made in the
-- src:1347 | proceedings —
-- src:1349 | (a) for such time and on such terms as the Court thinks fit; and
-- src:1351 | (b) from time to time until it appears that the cause of inability
-- src:1352 | has ceased.
@ref s 43(2)(a) and (b) (src:1341-1352)
GIVEN `it appears to the satisfaction of a District Court that a party is unable from any cause to pay a sum recovered against the party or an instalment of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court, in its discretion, decides to suspend or stay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(2) the District Court may suspend or stay the judgment or order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at any time it appears to the satisfaction of a District Court that any party ... is unable from any cause to pay ..., the Court may, in its discretion, suspend or stay" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        IF NOT (`it appears to the satisfaction of a District Court that a party is unable from any cause to pay a sum recovered against the party or an instalment of it`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the Court, in its discretion, decides to suspend or stay` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, in its discretion"; the judgment is the Court's
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1357 | (3) Where an order for payment by instalments is made, the
-- src:1358 | payment is to be made into court and no enforcement may issue,
-- src:1359 | except with the permission of the District Court.
@ref s 43(3) (src:1357-1359)
GIVEN `an order for payment by instalments is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the District Court has given permission to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(3) enforcement may issue` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on enforcement "Where an order for payment by instalments is made"; where none is made the subsection says nothing of enforcement
        IF NOT (`an order for payment by instalments is made`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no enforcement may issue, except with the permission of the District Court"; with permission the bar is lifted and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA); the power to enforce is section 44
        IF `the District Court has given permission to enforce` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no enforcement may issue, except with the permission of the District Court"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 43(3) (src:1357-1359)
GIVEN `an order for payment by instalments is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the District Court has given permission to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(3) the bar on enforcement applies` MEANS
    IF `an order for payment by instalments is made` AND NOT (`the District Court has given permission to enforce`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is on enforcement "Where an order for payment by instalments is made ... except with the permission of the District Court" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE; with permission the bar is lifted)
         JUST FALSE

@ref s 43(3) (src:1357-1359)
GIVEN `an order for payment by instalments is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 43(3) the payment is to be made into court` MEANS
    IF `an order for payment by instalments is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order for payment by instalments is made, the payment is to be made into court" (this subsection requires no payment into court on these facts; a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

-- src:1365 | 44. Subject to section 43(3), a judgment or an order of a District
-- src:1366 | Court may be enforced in any manner prescribed by Rules of Court.
@ref s 44 (src:1365-1366)
GIVEN `the manner is prescribed by Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 43(3) bars enforcement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 44 the judgment or order of a District Court may be enforced in the manner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to section 43(3)"; where that subsection bars enforcement, this section grants nothing (see s 43(3))
        IF `section 43(3) bars enforcement` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the manner is prescribed by Rules of Court` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of enforcement "in any manner prescribed by Rules of Court"; Rules of Court are not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1370 | 45.—(1) If a judgment or order of a District Court is for the
-- src:1371 | execution of a deed, or signing of a document, or for the indorsement
-- src:1372 | of a negotiable instrument, and the party ordered to execute, sign or
-- src:1373 | indorse such instrument is absent, neglects or refuses to do so, any
-- src:1374 | party interested in having the same executed, signed or indorsed,
-- src:1375 | may —
-- src:1377 | (a) prepare a deed, document or indorsement of the instrument
-- src:1378 | in accordance with the terms of the judgment or order; and
-- src:1380 | (b) tender the same to a District Court for execution upon the
-- src:1381 | proper stamp, if any is required by law,
-- src:1383 | and the signature thereof by the registrar, by order of the District
-- src:1384 | Court, has the same effect as the execution, signing or indorsement
-- src:1385 | thereof by the party ordered to execute.
@ref s 45(1)(a) and (b) (src:1370-1385)
GIVEN `the judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party ordered to execute, sign or indorse is absent, neglects or refuses to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party interested in having the instrument executed, signed or indorsed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(1) the interested party may prepare the instrument and tender it to a District Court for execution` MEANS
    IF `the judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument`
       AND `the party ordered to execute, sign or indorse is absent, neglects or refuses to do so`
       AND `the person is a party interested in having the instrument executed, signed or indorsed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a judgment or order ... is for the execution of a deed ..., and the party ordered ... is absent, neglects or refuses to do so, any party interested ... may" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
         JUST FALSE

@ref s 45(1) (src:1370-1385)
GIVEN `the registrar signs by order of the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(1) the signature has the same effect as the execution, signing or indorsement by the party ordered to execute` MEANS
    IF `the registrar signs by order of the District Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the effect is of "the signature thereof by the registrar, by order of the District Court"; another signature is not mentioned
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1387 | (2) Nothing in this section shall be held to abridge the powers of a
-- src:1388 | District Court to proceed by attachment against any person neglecting
-- src:1389 | or refusing to execute, sign or indorse any such instrument.
@ref s 45(2) (src:1387-1389)
GIVEN `the power is to proceed by attachment against a person neglecting or refusing to execute, sign or indorse an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 45(2) section 45 abridges the powers of a District Court` MEANS
    IF `the power is to proceed by attachment against a person neglecting or refusing to execute, sign or indorse an instrument`
    THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section shall be held to abridge the powers of a District Court to proceed by attachment against any person neglecting or refusing to execute, sign or indorse any such instrument"
         JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about the power to proceed by attachment and says nothing of any other power
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 48 to 49B -- appeals, stays and oral hearings`

-- src:1408 | 48.—(1) An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a
-- src:1409 | District Court exercising civil jurisdiction, where the parties have
-- src:1410 | agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the
-- src:1411 | decision is final, unless the party seeking to appeal proves that —
-- src:1413 | (a) the decision is affected by fraud or illegality; or
-- src:1415 | (b) there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural
-- src:1416 | justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision.
@ref s 48(1)(a) and (b) (src:1408-1416)
GIVEN `the parties agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party seeking to appeal proves that there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) an appeal can be brought against the decision of a District Court exercising civil jurisdiction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on an appeal "where the parties have agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final"; without that agreement the subsection says nothing of whether an appeal can be brought (the right of appeal is s 47 and the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969)
        IF NOT (`the parties agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the party seeking to appeal proves that — (a) ...; or (b) ..."; where the party proves fraud, illegality or a fundamental breach of natural justice the bar is lifted and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA)
        IF `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` OR `the party seeking to appeal proves that there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a District Court exercising civil jurisdiction, where the parties have agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final, unless ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 48(1) (src:1408-1416)
GIVEN `the parties agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party seeking to appeal proves that there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) the bar on an appeal applies to the decision` MEANS
    IF `the parties agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final`
       AND NOT (`the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` OR `the party seeking to appeal proves that there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is "where the parties have agreed in writing ... that the decision is final, unless" the appellant proves fraud, illegality or a fundamental breach (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE; "unless" lifts the bar)
         JUST FALSE

-- src:1418 | (2) An agreement mentioned in subsection (1) —
-- src:1420 | (a) may be made before or after the decision to which the
-- src:1421 | agreement relates is made; and
-- src:1423 | (b) may relate to part of a decision, in which case references in
-- src:1424 | subsection (1) to a decision are to be read as references to
-- src:1425 | that part of the decision.
@ref s 48(2)(a) (src:1418-1425)
GIVEN when IS A `When an agreement was made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2) an agreement mentioned in subsection (1) may be made at that time` MEANS
    CONSIDER when
    WHEN `Before the decision was made` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `After the decision was made` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says the agreement "may be made before or after the decision" and says nothing of any other time
    WHEN `At another time` THEN NOTHING

@ref s 48(2)(b) (src:1418-1425)
GIVEN `the agreement relates to part of a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2) the references in subsection (1) to a decision are references to that part of the decision` MEANS
    IF `the agreement relates to part of a decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in which case" - the reading as that part applies where the agreement relates to part of a decision; for an agreement about the whole decision the paragraph is silent
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1431 | 49.—(1) An appeal from a District Court exercising civil
-- src:1432 | jurisdiction does not operate as a stay of execution or enforcement
