GIVEN `the District Court or the General Division of the High Court has ordered a stay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(1) the appeal operates as a stay of execution or enforcement or of proceedings under the judgment or order appealed from` MEANS
    IF `the District Court or the General Division of the High Court has ordered a stay`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not operate as a stay ... unless the District Court or the General Division of the High Court so orders"; with an order the bar is lifted, and the stay then rests on the order, not on the appeal (QA: a lifted bar grants nothing)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal from a District Court exercising civil jurisdiction does not operate as a stay of execution or enforcement or of proceedings under the judgment or order appealed from"
         JUST FALSE

