    IF `the General Division of the High Court has directed that the intermediate act or proceeding is invalidated`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No intermediate act or proceeding is invalidated except so far as the General Division of the High Court may direct"; to the extent it directs, the bar is lifted and the invalidation rests on the direction (QA)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No intermediate act or proceeding is invalidated except so far as the General Division of the High Court may direct"
         JUST FALSE

