        IF NOT (`oral evidence is given during the part of the proceeding`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless all the parties consent" lifts the bar and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA)
        IF `all the parties consent` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not allow any part of a proceeding where oral evidence is given (including any part of a trial of an action) to be conducted without an oral hearing, unless all the parties consent"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 49A(2) (src:1453-1455)
