-- src:1478 | 49B.—(1) A District Judge sitting in a District Court may, on his or
-- src:1479 | her own motion, summarily dismiss any appeal made against a
-- src:1480 | decision of the registrar relating to civil proceedings, if the District
-- src:1481 | Judge is satisfied of any of the following:
-- src:1483 | (a) every issue in the appeal has already been decided by a
-- src:1484 | District Court or a higher court in an earlier matter in which
-- src:1485 | the appellant was involved, and the appeal therefore has no
-- src:1486 | merit;
-- src:1488 | (b) such conditions as may be prescribed by the Rules of Court
-- src:1489 | are met.
@ref s 49B(1)(a) and (b) (src:1478-1489)
GIVEN `the appeal is against a decision of the registrar relating to civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the District Judge is satisfied that every issue in the appeal has already been decided in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, and the appeal therefore has no merit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the District Judge is satisfied that the conditions prescribed by the Rules of Court are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49B(1) the District Judge may on his or her own motion summarily dismiss the appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any appeal made against a decision of the registrar relating to civil proceedings"
        IF NOT (`the appeal is against a decision of the registrar relating to civil proceedings`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the District Judge is satisfied that every issue in the appeal has already been decided in an earlier matter in which the appellant was involved, and the appeal therefore has no merit` OR `the District Judge is satisfied that the conditions prescribed by the Rules of Court are met` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may ... summarily dismiss ... if the District Judge is satisfied of any of the following" (a failed "if" is taken as the text's no: marginal reading (a)); also subject to subsection (2)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

